text After school, I go to the drama club room.
text I open the door like I usually do but find the room empty.
text I grab a chair and wait.
text Everyone else should be here soon.
text Kyou, Fujibayashi, Furukawa and... Kotomi.
text That's why I wait.
text Every time I hear a sound from the hallway, I partly open my eyes and look to the sliding door.
text No one shows up.
text It feels as if it were all a mirage.
text We were all orbiting around her.
text It was only two days ago.
text Kyou made impossible demands. Fujibayashi was kind and reserved. Furukawa was serious to a fault and tried her best at everything.
text Kotomi was becoming more and more cheerful. She shined so brightly in my eyes.
text I enjoyed being in that circle of friends.
text But now it all feels like something that happened long ago.
text Kotomi is still in that dark house.
text She's desperately clinging to a past to which she's chained.
text She's running away from the happiness she finally found.
text She's running away from her new life, her friends, and me.
text Kotomi is trying to leave everything behind.
text I need to find the words to explain.
text I need to find the exact words that can connect Kotomi to her future.
text How can I tell her?
text What can I say?
text I sit here with my mind still clouded, waiting.
