text When I arrive at Kotomi's house, it's already evening.
text The fading yellow light saturates the roof, walls, and windowsills.
text I press the doorbell.
text Two times, three times, four times...
text Nothing happens.
text I start to doubt if the bell even works.
text I look around but don't see light coming from any of the windows.
text Yet I know.
text Kotomi is inside, holding her breath like an injured stray cat.
text This door will not open from the outside.
text It's nobody's fault.
text Kotomi is only keeping her promise.
