text I follow the path to get into the garden.
text The chorus of insects echo like the night.
text The garden of Kotomi's childhood.
text Any lingering traces of the happy days of her past are completely gone.
text With no words or means to bring them back, I stand there in the overgrown grass.
text The plants have grown chaotically in neglect. Their names have long since been forgotten.
text They quietly surround me, as if to reproach the intruder.
text I place my fingers on the glass door that leads to the living room.
text It opened yesterday, but does not budge today.
